0008:     """
0009:     Fill each grey open-top frame with red and extend a red spill line above it toward its doubled top cap.
0010: 
0011:     Input structure
0012:     - The background is the dominant empty color.
0013:     - The only foreground color is grey.
0014:     - The grey pixels form one or more 4-connected rectangular frames with solid left, right, and bottom sides.
0015:     - Each frame's top side has exactly one background gap and a two-pixel grey cap on one side of that gap.
0016: 
0017:     Rule
0018:     - Preserve all grey pixels.
0019:     - For each frame, color the background pixels inside the frame and the missing top pixel red.
0020:     - On the row just above the frame, draw red from the top gap to the grid edge in the direction of the two-pixel cap.
0021: 
0022:     Key insight
0023:     - The asymmetric two-pixel cap on the top edge marks the horizontal direction of the red spill ray.
0024:     """
0025:     g = np.asarray(grid, dtype=int)
0026:     bg = get_bg(g)
0027:     W = g.shape[1]
0028:     assert bg != Color.GREY
